Os9 kermit (Glen Seaton/Robert Larson) distribution file (07/02/85) (ral)  Read os9ker.bwr for known bugs and limitationsOs9 kermit compilation instructions:Compilation switches:  -dCOCO          Same as -dtps=60 -dnooverlap  -dtps=number    Set ticks per second.  Gotten from <time.h> in not defined.                  (<time.h> is often wrong or needs its own compilation switch.)  -dnooverlap     Specifies that disk i/o and serial i/o cannot occur at the                  same time.  Hopefully only needed for COCO.  Slows down                    transfer if not needed.  (Avoids timeouts if it is needed.)  -dticstosleep=number                  Specifies number of ticks to sleep between checking for                  input while waiting for packet.  Making it bigger makes                  timeouts more accurate.  Making it too big will slow file                  transfers.  Default value is 4, minimum is 1.  About 		  1/10 second is recommended.  -dtimeoutint=number                  Number of "seconds" until timeout.  (Inaccurate.)  Default                  15.      -f=kermit       Specifies name of compiled program.Compilation:CC os9ker.c os9get.c os9sen.c os9rec.c os9srv.c os9utl.c os9raw.c os9con.c         os9qui.c -f=kermit [other options]   By CC I mean cc1 or cc2 as appropriate, unless you were sensible andrenamed the appropriate one to cc.Distributing compiled version:  At this time, I will only distribute the .s file if there is a special request.Using coco version on other os9/6809 systems:  Should work, but switches described above are set for coco.Using on os9/68000:  I know of no reason this version will not work on os9/68000, however ithas not yet been tested.